Headless: text boxes' content

A frontend that draws text boxes (createTextEdit()) itself needs what each holds, and a way to give Mudlet what the
player types in it. THeadlessSession had neither: a script's getTextEditText() read the registry, but nothing told the
app the box's text, read-only state, placeholder, style sheet or Tab behaviour, and the null view dropped the
placeholder and Tab behaviour, and noted no change of the text, read-only state, placeholder or Tab behaviour.

This adds THeadlessSession::TextBoxContent (text, readOnly, placeholder, styleSheet, tabMovesFocus) and
textBoxContent(), as getTextEditText() and the setTextEdit*() functions read and set them; the null view keeps the
placeholder and Tab behaviour, and tells the session of each script setting, so a change names the box in
scriptWindowsChanged. setTextBoxText() is the player's typing: it sets the text as the GUI's box does as its text
changes, which raises no event, and is not told back. It is refused for a name that is no text box, for a box that is
read-only or not shown, and where runLua() is. Tested in HeadlessSessionWindowsTest, and described in
docs/headless.md beside labelContent().

Carried by Mudlet/android's scripts/apply-mudlet-patches.sh until Mudlet/Mudlet has it.

